R"VG(
# will_epitaph.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the will (someone old who will die within six years: `@cast will`) and the epitaph (a
# stone for someone dead within three: `@cast dead`; their death by its cause, `@death`, and a deed of their life, `@deed`). The will
# leaves the people's own things (their house as the ruins show it, their crop and herd, their craft's tools, their clothes and music)
# to the history's kin; the epitaph's lines keep the pronouns' reach (an inscription).

@root epitaph.by.* epitaph.deed.* sermon.* inscription.*

# ---- the will ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.will (words=34..140)
  (2) {@cast will}{will.open}\n{will.items}\n{will.close}
  {@cast will}{will.open}\n{will.items}\n{med.wi.last}\n{will.close}

will.open (formula)
  I, {$me:name} of {$me.home}, {will.state}, set down what is to be done with what is mine.
  This is the will of {$me:name}, {$me.trade} of {$me.home}, written in the {#year:ord} year of {city}.
  {$me:name}, {will.state}, to whoever reads this after me:
  The last wishes of {$me:name} of {$me.home}, {will.state}, in {season.now} of the year {#year:digits}:
  Before {god} and the scribe of {$me.home}, I, {$me:name}, {$me.trade}, leave what I have as follows.
  I, {$me:name}, {will.state}, having counted what I own and found it more than I thought:

will.state
  old and in my right mind
  sick in body and clear in head
  in my {#$me.age:ord} year
  ($me.age>=70) older than anyone I know
  with my eyes going and my memory not
  well enough to write and not to walk
  ($me.age>=60) old enough to stop pretending otherwise

will.items
  {will.item} {will.item} {will.item}
  {will.item} {will.item} {will.item} {will.item}
  (0.7) {will.item} {will.item}\n{med.wi.burial} {will.item}

will.item
  (2 once has:$spouse) To {$spouse}, {med.wi.house}, {med.wi.while}.
  (2 once has:$child) To {$child}, {med.wi.land}.
  (2 once has:$child) To {$child}, {med.wi.tools}, {med.wi.worth}
  (once has:$kin) To {$kin}, {med.wi.thing}, {med.wi.because}
  (once) To {holyplace}, {med.wi.tithe}
  (once) To my neighbour, {med.wi.borrowed}, with my apologies.
  (once) {med.wi.debt}
  (once) The {beast} is to go to whoever will feed it, and {med.wi.beast}.
  (once) Nobody is to quarrel over the {vessel}. There are enough {vessel} for everyone, and more than enough quarrels.
  (once) {med.wi.burial}
  (once age>=medieval) The deeds of the {med.wi.deeds} are with the {med.wi.keeper} of {$me.home}.
  (once stage>=1) If the house cannot be kept, sell it and go where there is {watersrc.n}; a house is only {walls.of}.
  (once has:$child) To {$child:obj} also, {garment}, which {med.wi.garment}.
  (once) Whoever in the family can play {instrument} is to have it; if nobody can, whoever wants to learn, and the {herd} will have to bear it.
  (once) My seat at {festival}, {med.wi.seat}, is to be kept empty for a {med.wi.span}, then given to {med.wi.youngest}.

med.wi.seat
  by the {fuel} fire
  under the {colour.holy} cloth
  nearest the {drink}
  at the end of the long table
  by {holyplace} door

med.wi.span
  year
  harvest
  round of the feasts
  whole turn of the seasons

med.wi.youngest
  the youngest
  whoever cooks
  the child who sings worst
  the first grandchild to ask for it

med.wi.house
  the house and everything in it
  (has:$me.home.landmark) {house.one} by {$me.home.landmark} and all that is in it
  the house, the {vessel} in the store and the {crop} in them
  the house under its {roofs}, which I mended twice and you mended once
  the house, the yard and the {tree.n} in it

med.wi.while
  for as long as {$spouse:name} lives
  and the right to sit in the sun at its door
  for life, and after that to the children
  and may it be warmer for you than it was for me

med.wi.land
  the {herd} and the upper field
  the {crop} field below {watersrc}, and the stones in it, which are many
  the {herd}, all of them, and the one with the bad leg especially
  the field of {crop2} and the right of way to it
  (coast=1|river=1) the boat, the nets and the place on the shore
  (has:$me.home.landmark) the strip of {crop} by {$me.home.landmark}, which my mother had from hers

med.wi.tools
  {tool} and the {craft}
  my {craft} and {tool} that goes with it
  the workshop and {tool}
  (age>=medieval) the loom, the {craft} and the customers

med.wi.worth
  and the knowing of it, which is worth more.
  which will feed {$child:obj} if {$child:name} keeps at it.
  and the patience, if I could leave that.
  since {$child:name} was always better at it than I said.

med.wi.thing
  the {colour.any} {garment.n} with the {motif.over.s} on it
  the {vessel.one.n} of {drink} that I was saving
  my {#n} {coin} in the {vessel.one.n} under the floor
  my place at the {craft}-house
  the good knife and the bad advice

med.wi.because
  because {$kin:name} asked for it, which nobody else did.
  because {$kin:name} came to see me in {season.now}, when it was hard to come.
  for the years of looking after me.
  and nothing else, and {$kin:name} knows why.

motif.over.s
  {med.motif.s}
med.motif.s
  (motif=lines) lines
  (motif=circles) circles
  (motif=steps) steps
  (motif=spirals) spirals
  (motif=glyphs) old signs
  (motif=figures) figures
  (motif=stars) stars

med.wi.tithe
  a tenth of the {crop}, for the lamps.
  {#n} {measure.load} of {crop} at every {festival} until it is used up.
  the {herd}'s firstborn for {#n|year}, as my mother gave.
  {#n} {coin}, to have my name said at {festival}.
  the best of the {fruit}, every year the tree bears.

med.wi.borrowed
  the {med.wi.tool} I borrowed and never returned
  the {vessel.one.n} I borrowed in the year of the flood
  the {med.wi.tool} I took and the {med.wi.tool} I meant to give back

med.wi.tool
  ladder
  saw
  good knife
  big pot
  hand cart
  awl
  sieve

med.wi.debt
  My debts are to be paid from the {crop} before anything else; there are fewer than people think.
  The {med.chr.trades.one} of {$me.home} owes me {#n} {coin}. Let it go; there are children there, and a {beast} that eats.
  I owe the {med.chr.trades.one} at {city2} for {vessel}. Pay it in {crop} if the {coin} are short; {med.chr.trades.one}s like {crop}.
  Whatever is owed to me is forgiven, except by the {med.chr.trades.one}, who knows why.

med.chr.trades.one
  weaver
  potter
  smith
  carter
  boatman
  dyer
  miller

med.wi.beast
  it bites, so be quick
  it will not like the change
  it is older than the children and should be treated so
  it eats {food}, whatever anyone tells you

med.wi.burial (share=0.6)
  I am to be {buried}, and no fuss, and no {drink} until it is done.
  Let {colour.mourn} be worn for {#n|day} and no longer; life is for the living.
  No {drink} at the burying, and plenty after.
  Lay me with {tool} and the {colour.holy} cloth, as is right.
  Let them sing the old song at {deadplace}, the short one, and stop before the {herd} come in.
  I am to be {buried} beside my mother, with my feet to {med.wi.face}.
  Carry me past the {craft}-house on the way to {deadplace}; I want to see the work stop for once.
  Put {food} and a {vessel.one.n} of {drink} in with me; it is a long road, they say, and no inns.
  Burn {fuel} at the door for three nights, and then let the fire go out and the house be yours.
  Let the {med.chr.trades} of {$me.home} carry me; they owe me that, and they know it.

med.wi.face
  {mountain}
  {river}
  the sunrise
  the house

med.wi.deeds
  house
  field
  mill
  boat shed
  workshop

med.wi.keeper
  scribe
  priest
  clerk
  elders

med.wi.garment
  my mother made and I never wore out
  is too good for me and always was
  will keep out {weather} if nothing else will

# a last word to the family (a sentence or two)
med.wi.last (share=0.5)
  To all of them, this: {proverb}.
  Keep to {virtue}, which I did not always.
  Do not grieve long; I did not like long things, except the {craft}.
  Sell the {herd} slowly and the {vessel} quickly; I have watched the market at {$me.home} for {#$me.age|year}.
  When you eat {food} at {festival}, eat my share, and complain about it the way I did.
  Look after the old ones on the hill; you will be one.
  {god.call}, and keep the lamp lit.
  I have had a good life, mostly, and a long one, entirely.
  Do not sell the {herd} to the first who asks; sell them to the second.
  {exclaim}, I have written more than I meant to.
  Plant {med.wi.plant} where I am, so I am some use.

med.wi.plant
  a {tree.n}
  {crop2}
  something that flowers

will.close (formula)
  Witnessed at {$me.home}, in {season.now}. {god.keep}.
  Sealed by my hand. {$me:name}.
  Let this stand. {$me:name}, {$me.trade}.
  Written for me by the scribe, read back to me, and true. {$me:name}.
  So I leave it. {$me:name}, of {$me.home}.

# ---- the epitaph ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.epitaph (words=9..58)
  {@cast dead}{epitaph.name}\n{@deed epitaph.deed}\n{@death epitaph.by}\n{epitaph.coda}
  {@cast dead}{epitaph.name}\n{@death epitaph.by}\n{epitaph.coda}

epitaph.name (formula)
  (age<=medieval $x.role!=ruler) {$x:name}, {$x.trade} of {$x.home}.
  ($x.role!=ruler) Here lies {$x:name}.
  (age>=industrial $x.role!=ruler) {$x:name}. {#$x.born:digits} to {#$x.died:digits}.
  ($x.role=ruler has:$x.reigned) {$x:full}, who ruled {#$x.reigned|year}.
  ($x.role=ruler !has:$x.reigned) {$x:full}.
  ($x.role=ruler has:$x.epithet) {$x:full} {$x.epithet}.
  ($x.role!=ruler) For {$x:name}, who lived {#$x.age|year}.
  ($x.role!=ruler has:$x.spouse) {$x:name}, {epitaph.spouseof} {$x.spouse:name}.
  ($x.role!=ruler) {$x:name} of {$x.home}, who {med.ep.was}.

med.ep.was
  kept the {craft}
  ($x.trait=kind) was kind
  ($x.trait=brave) was not afraid
  ($x.trait=pious) kept the faith
  ($x.trait=wise) knew things
  ($x.trait=proud) was proud of it
  was {#$x.age} and no more

epitaph.spouseof
  ($x.gender=she) wife of
  ($x.gender=he) husband of

epitaph.deed.built
  {$x:name} [cut the stone for|carried the stone for|worked on] {$d.work} at {$d.place}.
  {$x:name} raised {$d.work} at {$d.place}, and it stands.
epitaph.deed.battle
  {$x:name} [stood at|came home from] the battle of {$d.place}.
  {$x:name} was at {$d.place} when it was fought, and did not run.
epitaph.deed.founding
  {$x:name} was among the first families of {$d.place}.
  {$x:name} cleared the ground at {$d.place} with {med.ep.hands}.
epitaph.deed.deed
  {$x:name} {deed.short}.
epitaph.deed.invention
  {$x:name} made {$d.invention}.
epitaph.deed.discovery
  {$x:name} went where nobody had gone, and came back to tell it.
epitaph.deed.trade
  (2 $x.age>=16) {$x:name} {trade.main} {trade.tail}
  ($x.role=ruler) {$x:name} held the rule in peace and in war.
  ($x.age>=16) {$x:name} {med.ep.life}.
  ($x.age<16) {$x:name} {med.ep.child}.

med.ep.child
  was too young for a trade and old enough to be missed
  liked the {herd} better than the people, and the {herd} agreed
  could count to {#n} and counted everything
  sang the {festival} songs, all of them, wrong
  was learning the {craft}, and was quick at it

med.ep.hands
  bare hands
  {tool}
  {tool} and a temper

med.ep.life
  made {craft} that is still in use
  kept the {herd} and the peace
  fed the {bird} every winter
  ($x.children>=2) brought up {#$x.children|child} and buried none
  sang at every {festival} and was asked to stop at most of them
  knew every road between {$x.home} and {city2}

deed.short
  ($d.deed=song) made a song that is still sung
  ($d.deed=laws) gave the laws
  ($d.deed=map) drew the map of the land
  ($d.deed=healed) healed the sick
  ($d.deed=taught) taught the children of {$d.place}
  ($d.deed=book|$d.deed=chronicle) wrote what we read
  ($d.deed=hunt|$d.deed=sailed|$d.deed=frieze|$d.deed=theory|$d.deed=pictures|$d.deed=gardens) did what is remembered of {$x:obj}

trade.main
  was a {$x.trade} all {$x:poss} life
  ($x.age>=30) kept the {$x.trade}'s trade all {$x:poss} days
  was the best {$x.trade} in {$x.home}, and said so
  (age>=industrial) served {$x.home} as a {$x.trade}
  worked at {craft} in {$x.home} for {#$x.age|year}, near enough
trade.tail
  (2) .
  , and taught it to {$x:poss} children.
  , and never once complained, which nobody believed.
  ; the work outlasted {$x:obj}.

epitaph.by.sickness
  {$x:name} died of {$c.sickness}, with [the others|the rest of the street|{$x:poss} neighbours].
  {$x:name} died in the sickness of the year {#$c.year:digits}.
  {$c.sickness} took {$x:name} in {season.now}.
epitaph.by.battle
  {$x:name} fell at {$c.place}, in {$c.war}.
  {$x:name} did not come back from {$c.place}.
epitaph.by.famine
  {$x:name} died in the hunger of the year {#$c.year:digits}.
  {$x:name} gave {$x:poss} bread to the children in the hungry year, and died of it.
epitaph.by.flood
  The water took {$x:name} in the flood of the year {#$c.year:digits}.
epitaph.by.quake
  {$x:name} died when the ground shook at {$c.place}.
epitaph.by.sack
  {$x:name} died when {$c.place} burned.
epitaph.by.impact
  {$x:name} died when the stone fell from the sky.
epitaph.by.eruption
  {$x:name} died under the ash of {mountain}.
epitaph.by.young
  {$x:name} lived {#$x.age|year}.
  {$x:name} was {#$x.age} and wanted to be older.
  {$x:name} was too small for this stone.
epitaph.by.old
  {$x:name} {old.main} {old.tail}
epitaph.by.illness
  {$x:name} {ill.main} {ill.tail}
epitaph.by.childbirth
  {$x:name} died bringing a child into the world, and the child lived.
epitaph.by.accident
  {$x:name} died by a fall, at {#$x.age}, which was nobody's fault and everybody's grief.
epitaph.by.fire
  {$x:name} died in the fire, going back in for the {beast}.
epitaph.by.cold
  {$x:name} died in the cold, a mile from home.
epitaph.by.sea
  The sea took {$x:name}. This stone has no one under it.
epitaph.by.murdered
  {$x:name} was killed, and the one who did it {med.ep.killer}.
epitaph.by.any
  {$x:name} died in {$x.home}, in {season.now}.
  {$x:name} has {death.went}.

med.ep.killer
  is known to {god}
  was never found
  was hanged at {$x.home}

old.main
  lived {#$x.age|year}
  saw {#$x.age} harvests
  lived to be old, {simile},
  buried {$x:poss} friends and outlived {$x:poss} enemies
  (moons>0) saw {moon} full a thousand times
  kept {$x:poss} wits to the last
  lived {#$x.age|year} and complained of every one
old.tail
  and died in {$x:poss} [bed|sleep|own house].
  and died with {$x:poss} children round {$x:obj}.
  and went quietly.
  , and was not ready to go.
  , and has {death.went}.

ill.main
  was taken by a fever {=.quick}
  was ill a long time and bore it {=.long}
  died young, at {#$x.age}, {=.unnamed}
  sickened in {season.now} {=.unnamed}
  (age>=industrial) was taken by the cough {=.quick}
ill.tail
  (.quick=1) in {$x:poss} {#$x.age:ord} year.
  (.long=1) , and died at {#$x.age}.
  (.unnamed=1) , and nobody knows of what.
  (.quick=1) , and was gone in [three|nine] days.
  (.long=1) , and never complained.

epitaph.coda (formula)
  {god} keep {$x:obj}.
  (has:$x.spouse) {$x.spouse:name} set this stone.
  (has:$x.child) {$x.child:name} set this stone.
  (age>=industrial) [Rest.|Not lost, gone before.|The work is done.|Asleep.]
  (age<=medieval) [We cut this so that you are not forgotten.|The stone remembers.|Under {skyone}, at rest.]
  (moons>0) {moon} keeps the watch now.
  (deadway!=none) Laid in {deadplace} with {$x:poss} people.
  The dead are {dead.are}.
  We wore {colour.mourn} for {$x:obj}.
)VG"
